{#
  What may be sent. A closed list is only fair if it can be read, so metrics answers it
  and this page prints it. It is the page to open when a measurement was refused: the
  dimension that was wrong, or the value a closed dimension does not allow, is on it.

  Expected: view (src/views/vocabulary.js buildVocabulary), plus the shell's own.
#}{% extends "layout.njk" %}

{% block title %}vocabulary — webtools metrics{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<h1>Vocabulary</h1>
<p class="subtitle">{{ view.metricsText }} metrics. A name that is not here is refused with a <code>400</code>, and so is a dimension a metric does not declare.</p>

<section>
  <h2>Who may send</h2>
  {%- if view.subsystems.length %}
  <p class="chooser">{% for subsystem in view.subsystems %}<span class="current">{{ subsystem }}</span>{% endfor %}</p>

  {%- else %}
  <p class="absent">The vocabulary could not be read.</p>
  {%- endif %}
</section>

<section>
  <h2>The metrics</h2>
  {%- if not view.metrics.length %}
  <p class="absent">No metric could be read.</p>
  {%- else %}
  <table class="grid vocabulary">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>metric</th><th>required</th><th>optional</th><th>may carry</th><th>project</th><th></th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {%- for metric in view.metrics %}
      <tr>
        <th class="mono">{{ metric.name }}</th>
        <td>
          {%- if metric.required.length %}
          {%- for dimension in metric.required %}
          <span class="dim"><span class="name">{{ dimension.name }}</span>{% if dimension.open %}<span class="open" title="the values cannot be listed in advance: only the key is closed">open</span>{% else %}{{ dimension.values | join(" · ") }}{% endif %}</span>
          {%- endfor %}
          {%- else %}<span class="absent">none</span>{% endif %}
        </td>
        <td>
          {%- if metric.optional.length %}
          {%- for dimension in metric.optional %}
          <span class="dim"><span class="name">{{ dimension.name }}</span>{% if dimension.open %}<span class="open">open</span>{% else %}{{ dimension.values | join(" · ") }}{% endif %}</span>
          {%- endfor %}
          {%- else %}<span class="absent">none</span>{% endif %}
        </td>
        <td>{% if metric.values.length %}{% for value in metric.values %}<code>{{ value }}</code> {% endfor %}{% else %}<span class="absent">count only</span>{% endif %}</td>
        <td>{% if metric.project %}yes{% else %}<span class="absent">no</span>{% endif %}</td>
        <td><a href="/daily?metric={{ metric.name }}">buckets &rarr;</a></td>
      </tr>
      {%- endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note"><strong>required</strong>: without it the measurement is refused.
    <strong>optional</strong>: it exists only in some cases, and absent is absent.
    <strong>open</strong>: the values cannot be listed, the key is closed.
    <strong>project</strong>: a measurement of it may name a project, and then it lands in that project's accumulator too.</p>
  {%- endif %}
</section>
{% endblock %}
